- Output validation.

## B. YouTube Data API v3 — Required

Base URL:
`https://www.googleapis.com/youtube/v3`

Methods:

| Method | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `channels.list` | Channel profile and public details |
| `videos.list` | Video metadata and public statistics |
| `playlistItems.list` | Channel upload history |
| `search.list` | Public video and channel discovery |
| `commentThreads.list` | Public video comments |
| `comments.list` | Comment replies where available |

Use:
- Channel ID.
- Video ID.
- Playlist ID.
- Pagination tokens.
- Published timestamps.
- Public statistics.

Important: Search API quota is limited. Cache results and control repeated searches.

## C. YouTube Analytics API — Required for Private Analytics

Base URL:
`https://youtubeanalytics.googleapis.com/v2`

Main method:
- `reports.query`

Use supported combinations of:
- Metrics.
- Dimensions.
- Date ranges.
- Filters.
- Sorting.

Examples of analytics:
- Views.
- Watch time.
- Average view duration.
- Likes.
- Comments.
- Shares.
- Subscribers gained.

Request only metrics and dimensions that the selected report supports.

## D. Google OAuth 2.0 — Required

Purpose:
- Secure Google account authorization.
- Channel connection.
- YouTube Analytics access.
- Token refresh.
- Permission revocation.

Use minimum required scopes:

Identity:
- `openid`
- `email`
- `profile`

YouTube public/private channel access:
- `https://www.googleapis.com/auth/youtube.readonly`

Analytics:
- `https://www.googleapis.com/auth/yt-analytics.readonly`

Do not request channel-management or publishing permissions in the initial beta.

Use incremental authorization when adding optional permissions later.

## E. Firebase Authentication — Required

Purpose:
- User login.
- Google sign-in.
- Email authentication.
- Session identity.
- Account management.

## F. Cloud Firestore — Required

Purpose:
- User profiles.
- Channel profiles.
- Projects.
- Ideas.
- Scripts.
- Research reports.
- Analytics snapshots.
- Preferences.
- Usage records.

## G. Firebase Cloud Storage — Required where files are needed

Purpose:
- Uploaded assets.
- Generated thumbnails.
- Audio files.
- Exported reports.
